{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":134871,"duration_api_ms":131568,"ttft_ms":1785,"ttft_stream_ms":1234,"time_to_request_ms":14,"num_turns":24,"result":"Clean. Here's a summary of the change:\n\n## Summary\n\nExtended `salt/beacons/diskusage.py` to support a \"usage dropped below expected\" alert alongside the existing \"usage rose above threshold\" alert, per mount.\n\n**Backward compatibility:** the existing bare-percentage config (`- /: 63%`) is untouched in code path and output — it's still treated as a maximum-only threshold and emits the exact same `{\"diskusage\": ..., \"mount\": ...}` dict as before.\n\n**New capability:** a mount's value can now be a mapping with `minimum` and/or `maximum` keys:\n```yaml\nbeacons:\n  diskusage:\n    - /: 63%                          # unchanged, existing behavior\n    - /mnt/nfs:\n        minimum: 10%\n        maximum: 90%\n    - /mnt/backup:\n        minimum: 5%                   # only alert on the \"vanished\" case\n```\n- `maximum` behaves identically to the legacy scalar form.\n- `minimum` fires when usage falls to or below it, tagging the event with `\"below_minimum\": True` so reactors can distinguish it from a high-usage alert.\n- `validate()` rejects a mapping that has neither key.\n\nAdded 4 new unit tests (`test_invalid_min_max_config`, `test_diskusage_minimum_match`, `test_diskusage_minimum_nomatch`, `test_diskusage_minimum_and_maximum`) plus a changelog fragment (`changelog/69890.added.md`) and doc updates in the beacon's docstring. All 14 tests in `tests/pytests/unit/beacons/test_diskusage.py` pass, including all pre-existing ones unchanged.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a668e73d-c686-4f92-a0bb-1956286f50ea","total_cost_usd":0.7351527000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":39,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41248,"cache_read_input_tokens":1011359,"output_tokens":12276,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"st